From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:36:47 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Meridian: no Mac-only words in the UI Windows shows too
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Windows people read "your Mac", ⌘ and Finder in screens shared with the Mac.
Now each such text is behind a Mac check, or says it the neutral way:
- the keychain errors (Ask keys, cloud keys, the custom AI, the Workbench
  vault) name the system's secure storage off the Mac;
- Mission Control's assistant is "Ctrl+J Assistant", the agent tab is "On
  this computer", and the first-session toast asks about Allow only on the
  Mac;
- Settings: the online-AI note and "It answers in ⌘T and ⌘J" go through
  keyText(); uploads come "from this computer"; Arc's passwords note only on
  the Mac says the Mac asks;
- the download's "Show in Finder" is "Show in folder" elsewhere;
- the tour's Full Disk Access and keychain cards are Mac-only in the
  template too, and the sign-in step says "on this computer".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
